1 NOTE Ahnentafel position 24.
1 NOTE Birth year confirmed as 1845 by his own baptism (PAR-0022): entry Nº 5, fol. 59, N.S. Mãe de Deus, Povoação (DGS 5228858 img 63). The act reads "nasceu em vinte [e] quatro do [?] mez oito[centos] quarenta e cinco" — day 24, year 1845; the month is illegible. This corrects the c.1847 estimate derived from his death record's stated age (PAR-0007) and the FS profile's unsubstantiated 1864 date.
1 NOTE His son Deocleciano's 1892 Sapucaia baptism (PAR-0004) records the father as "João Muniz Bitencourt", settling the José-vs-João question (the 1882 provisão PAR-0001 had recorded "José"). Both spellings are preserved.
1 NOTE Origin RESOLVED (31 July 2026): his own 1915 Carangola death register (PAR-0007 → event E-0036) records him "natural da Ilha de São Miguel" (Açores, Portugal), died 12 September 1915 aged 68 (born c.1847), married to Suzana Rita Brandão, leaving eleven children. He was himself the Azorean immigrant — which is why the Sapucaia baptism books (1856-1877) held no baptism for his generation. Nationality is therefore Portuguese (a documented birthplace, not a surname inference). This supersedes the earlier "unset origin" and resolves material conflict 6; note the óbito's c.1847 birth corrects the FamilySearch profile's unproved 1864 date.
1 NOTE Parents identified (1 August 2026) from his father's own 1866 Povoação death (PAR-0015): father Manoel Muniz Bytancourt (P-0042) — correcting the "Manoel Luiz Bittencourt" of the 1915 óbito (PAR-0007) — and, indirectly, mother Francisca Roza do Espirito Santo (P-0047), Manoel's wife and mother of his "oito filhos" (family F-0020, strong-evidence for João's maternity). His Azorean grandparents were João Muniz Bytancourt (P-0048) and Maria Jacintha de Medeiros (P-0049) of Nossa Senhora Mãe de Deus, Povoação, Ilha de São Miguel (family F-0023) — the line's furthest documented Açorean generation. The earlier collaborative-profile 1871 naturalisation link remains an unverified lead.
