1 TITL Parish baptism register entry of "Roza" (Rosa Eugenia de Lemos), 1835, Matriz de São João Batista de Itaboraí, naming her parents Manoel de Lemos [Pereira] and Maria Thereza de Jesus
1 TEXT The 1835 Itaboraí baptism of a girl "Roza", legitimate daughter of Manoel de Lemos [Pereira] (P-0052) and Maria Thereza de Jesus (P-0053), both natural of the parish; godparents Manoel José da Silva and Flor de Maria da Conceição. Taken to be the baptism of Rosa Eugenia de Lemos (P-0035), wife of Francisco José Bohrer: she is the only "Roza" of this exact couple across the browsed 1832-1838 Itaboraí baptisms, in the parish where her 1879 marriage justification was held (PAR-0002, "em casa do pai de José Antunes de Lemos") and matching the Lemos-Itaboraí family named as her brother "Candido Pereira de Lemos" in her husband's 1888 will (PRB-0005). The register wrote only the forename "Roza"; the identity is therefore a strong indirect match, not a direct statement of "Eugenia de Lemos".
